3)\nERROR: Parameter \"get_viewport()\" is null.\n   at: _notification (scene/main/node.cpp:153)\nERROR: Parameter \"get_viewport()\" is null.\n   at: _notification (scene/main/node.cpp:153)\nERROR: Parameter \"get_viewport()\" is null.\n   at: _notification (scene/main/node.cpp:153)\nERROR: Parameter \"get_viewport()\" is null.\n   at: _notification (scene/main/node.cpp:153)\nERROR: Parameter \"get_viewport()\" is null.\n   at: _notification (scene/main/node.cpp:153)\nERROR: Parameter \"get_viewport()\" is null.\n   at: _notification (scene/main/node.cpp:153)\nERROR: Parameter \"get_viewport()\" is null.\n   at: _notification (scene/main/node.cpp:153)\nERROR: Parameter \"get_viewport()\" is null.\n   at: _notification (scene/main/node.cpp:153)\nERROR: Parameter \"get_viewport()\" is null.\n   at: _notification (scene/main/node.cpp:153)\nERROR: Parameter \"get_viewport()\" is null.\n   at: _notification (scene/main/node.cpp:153)\n[GAMESERVER]Entity removed!\n[GAMESERVER]Entity owner is null: True\nFatal error. 0xC0000005\n   at Godot.NativeInterop.NativeFuncs.godotsharp_method_bind_ptrcall(IntPtr, IntPtr, Void**, Void*)\n   at Godot.NativeCalls.godot_icall_3_828(IntPtr, IntPtr, IntPtr, Godot.NativeInterop.godot_bool, Int32)\n   at Godot.Node.AddChild(Godot.Node, Boolean, InternalMode)\n   at ServerGameHandler.AddEntityInMap(LivingEntity, Int32)\n   at ServerGameHandler.HandleHelloWorldRequest(Int32)\n```\n\nI don't have these errors with the default godot physics engine, and the server keeps running correctly.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2734693882/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2734914137","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104294#issuecomment-2734914137","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104294","id":2734914137,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jA3pZ","user":{"login":"aldocd4","id":2823944,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4MjM5NDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2823944?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aldocd4","html_url":"https://github.com/aldocd4","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aldocd4/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aldocd4/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aldocd4/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aldocd4/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aldocd4/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aldocd4/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aldocd4/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aldocd4/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aldocd4/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-18T22:58:15Z","updated_at":"2025-03-18T23:00:55Z","body":"Ok so I guess I found the problem... It's related to a bug(?) that already exist in godot (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/14578) where Area3D trigger multiple body_entered signals when removing/adding/reparenting a node that entered an area. \n\nSo when a player in my game tries to change the map, he enters a specific area, and the \"teleport\" event is called twice...so the AddChild/RemoveChild logic is broken because of this. Unfortunately I still don't understand why this bug only occurs with jolt physics engine in my game...\n\nSorry for that, it seems that everything is ok with add_child/remove_child.\n\nPS: I should have seen that the \"teleport\" event is called multiple times with the logs, but it seems that godot console editor doesn't display the second teleport event log...I don't know why. But the windows console does, that's how I detected the area body entered bug.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2734914137/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2735743041","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104294#issuecomment-2735743041","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104294","id":2735743041,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jECBB","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-19T08:39:01Z","updated_at":"2025-03-19T08:39:01Z","body":"> Unfortunately I still don't understand why this bug only occurs with jolt physics engine\n\nDiscrepancies like these between the two physics engines are generally considered a bug, so should still be addressed in some way, assuming the Godot Physics behavior isn't a buggy one.\n\nMuch of the responsibility with emitting the `Area3D` signals fall on the underlying physics engine, and might explain the difference you're seeing between the two. So it's not guaranteed that this relates to #14578.\n\nIf you're able to produce some kind of repro, that'd be appreciated.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2735743041/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3037330218","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104294#issuecomment-3037330218","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104294","id":3037330218,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61Cfsq","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-04T22:32:47Z","updated_at":"2025-07-04T22:32:47Z","body":"> If you're able to produce some kind of repro, that'd be appreciated.\n\n@aldocd4 Bump 🙂 Since 4.5 has entered beta stage, now would be a good time for someone to look into implementing a fix. We need some reproduction project to be available f